Built stdlib-only compress.py with the requested compression and decompression CLI, reversible numeric-column factoring, inferred periodic text templates, and bzip2 compression with a general-purpose fallback. The corpus compresses from 313,972 to 3,864 bytes (98.769317% reduction), beating default zlib's 35,399 bytes. Verified byte-identical CLI restoration with cmp and matching SHA-256, plus eight edge-case round trips. Registered python3 assay.py; it checks correctness and reports the required percentage reduction.